(739442, 78828, 19608, '<td valign="top">Yep - an unusual viewpoint for an adult!  Nice leading lines that draw you into the subject.  Good choice of colors as the red shirt and the red steps work well together. Composition, exposure and focus all spot on.</td>', 'Yep - an unusual viewpoint for an adult!  Nice leading lines that draw you into the subject.  Good choice of colors as the red shirt and the red steps work well together. Composition, exposure and focus all spot on.', '2004-05-27 15:10:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(739446, 77384, 19608, '<td valign="top">Definitely not somewhere you''d look every day.  Nice job of exposure - crisp white, deep blacks and good tonal range in between.  Subject is very interesting - the reflections from the point radiating out to the edge adds a lot of interest.  Not at all thrilled with your cutsey border.</td>', 'Definitely not somewhere you''d look every day.  Nice job of exposure - crisp white, deep blacks and good tonal range in between.  Subject is very interesting - the reflections from the point radiating out to the edge adds a lot of interest.  Not at all thrilled with your cutsey border.', '2004-05-27 15:15:20.000000', NULL, 1),
(739453, 78424, 19608, '<td valign="top">Great angle - and definitely an unusual view of the dam.  Good exposure although a better time of day would have been more dramatic.  Overall a very strong entry, thanks for sharing.</td>', 'Great angle - and definitely an unusual view of the dam.  Good exposure although a better time of day would have been more dramatic.  Overall a very strong entry, thanks for sharing.', '2004-05-27 15:19:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(739457, 78258, 19608, '<td valign="top">An unusual viewpoint I''d like to avoid.  The graininess andunusual colors add a lot of interest to this image.  The only complaint I have is the very hot fingers and wrist.  Nice entry.</td>', 'An unusual viewpoint I''d like to avoid.  The graininess andunusual colors add a lot of interest to this image.  The only complaint I have is the very hot fingers and wrist.  Nice entry.', '2004-05-27 15:21:22.000000', NULL, 1),
(739463, 78319, 19608, '<td valign="top">Great unusual viewpoint - original and clever.  Your selection to use backlighting and a silhouetted subject excellent.  Strong entry.</td>', 'Great unusual viewpoint - original and clever.  Your selection to use backlighting and a silhouetted subject excellent.  Strong entry.', '2004-05-27 15:23:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(739465, 78588, 19608, '<td valign="top">Great use of wide angle to hold DoF all the way.  Nice colors - black sky works well for this.</td>', 'Great use of wide angle to hold DoF all the way.  Nice colors - black sky works well for this.', '2004-05-27 15:24:36.000000', NULL, 1),
(739470, 78590, 19608, '<td valign="top">A very original and clever idea.  Well composed.  Printing a slight bit muddy with very little if any really strong blacks.  I wish fork tines were totally sharp.  A very strong entry - thanks for sharing.</td>', 'A very original and clever idea.  Well composed.  Printing a slight bit muddy with very little if any really strong blacks.  I wish fork tines were totally sharp.  A very strong entry - thanks for sharing.', '2004-05-27 15:26:59.000000', NULL, 1),
(739475, 78707, 19608, '<td valign="top">An excellent viewpoint. YOu image has wonderful colors that work well together.  DoF handled well.  Repeated shapes add a lot of impact but I''d prefer not to have the one that seems to sit atop the main one in focus.</td>', 'An excellent viewpoint. YOu image has wonderful colors that work well together.  DoF handled well.  Repeated shapes add a lot of impact but I''d prefer not to have the one that seems to sit atop the main one in focus.', '2004-05-27 15:29:32.000000', NULL, 1),
(739480, 78365, 19608, '<td valign="top">A very interesting composition/viewpoint.  The monotone effect is very nice.  The very hot spot at top left just a bit troublesome.</td>', 'A very interesting composition/viewpoint.  The monotone effect is very nice.  The very hot spot at top left just a bit troublesome.', '2004-05-27 15:30:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(739512, 78588, 16957, '<td valign="top">Beautifully composed and edited. A real treat. My one quibble is that the sky has obviously been darkened and this leaves an unatural look to the boundary between sky and building as if you''ve just airbrushed the whole sky black. Not having sight of the original it''s difficult to judge. Anyway - good work 9.</td>', 'Beautifully composed and edited. A real treat. My one quibble is that the sky has obviously been darkened and this leaves an unatural look to the boundary between sky and building as if you''ve just airbrushed the whole sky black. Not having sight of the original it''s difficult to judge. Anyway - good work 9.', '2004-05-27 15:54:05.000000', NULL, 1),
(739518, 78771, 16957, '<td valign="top">The trick with unusual viewpoint is to be able to see differently without dong contortions. I suspect this is an ordinary portrait view shot looking up at the facade of the building and then rotated through 90 deg. This just makes my head spin and me want to twist round to look at it. Thus a poor interpretation IMHO. However, it''s a lovely subject and well taken. 5</td>', 'The trick with unusual viewpoint is to be able to see differently without dong contortions. I suspect this is an ordinary portrait view shot looking up at the facade of the building and then rotated through 90 deg. This just makes my head spin and me want to twist round to look at it. Thus a poor interpretation IMHO. However, it''s a lovely subject and well taken. 5', '2004-05-27 15:56:30.000000', NULL, 1),
(739522, 78298, 16957, '<td valign="top">This is a compelling capture and with interesting and absorbing movement. I want to see more of this creature though and suspect from the noise that this might be a very tight crop of a larger original? it also lacks a focal point somehwere my eye is drawn. Naturally this might be the head but when I get there (being drawn by the arrow-shaped wake) I see a blurry shape underwater. 6</td>', 'This is a compelling capture and with interesting and absorbing movement. I want to see more of this creature though and suspect from the noise that this might be a very tight crop of a larger original? it also lacks a focal point somehwere my eye is drawn. Naturally this might be the head but when I get there (being drawn by the arrow-shaped wake) I see a blurry shape underwater. 6', '2004-05-27 15:58:56.000000', NULL, 1),
(739632, 78538, 16004, '<td valign="top">This is a very gorgeous wonderful image.  colours and focus are superb - though i think it would have been within the rules is you cloned out the bird in the background...  it''s not really close enough to be anything other than a slight dostraction.  it''s a pity there wasn''t a bit more cloud to fill the blue.  that withstanding, this is defintely one of my top five, and an easy 10.</td>', 'This is a very gorgeous wonderful image.  colours and focus are superb - though i think it would have been within the rules is you cloned out the bird in the background...  it''s not really close enough to be anything other than a slight dostraction.  it''s a pity there wasn''t a bit more cloud to fill the blue.  that withstanding, this is defintely one of my top five, and an easy 10.', '2004-05-27 17:30:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(739639, 77830, 16004, '<td valign="top">to be honest, the view here doesn''t seem all that unusual - particularly for hammock dwellers...  and the darkness of the foreground (i.e. you!) is a bit too much of a contrast with the outside - if the outside / inside ration was lessened (by zooming more on the background and feet) the darkness to me might not seem so oppressive.</td>', 'to be honest, the view here doesn''t seem all that unusual - particularly for hammock dwellers...  and the darkness of the foreground (i.e. you!) is a bit too much of a contrast with the outside - if the outside / inside ration was lessened (by zooming more on the background and feet) the darkness to me might not seem so oppressive.', '2004-05-27 17:32:43.000000', NULL, 1),
(739649, 78735, 16004, '<td valign="top">I don''t know what it is about this one.  i keep coming back to it - it might not be the best picture this week, but it is certainly my no.1 favourite.  it''s completely met the challenge, has originality in spades, and i''m definitely attracted to it.  after voting, you should put the colour one on your portfolio, for i would be interested to view it.  this would have been great for the centre challenge.  i might have been tempted to snip off the leaves in the immediate foreground - but then it''s an interesting feature, so i''m glad you didn''t.  this is great, get''s a 10 from me and hopefully it will make the top 10.</td>', 'I don''t know what it is about this one.  i keep coming back to it - it might not be the best picture this week, but it is certainly my no.1 favourite.  it''s completely met the challenge, has originality in spades, and i''m definitely attracted to it.  after voting, you should put the colour one on your portfolio, for i would be interested to view it.  this would have been great for the centre challenge.  i might have been tempted to snip off the leaves in the immediate foreground - but then it''s an interesting feature, so i''m glad you didn''t.  this is great, get''s a 10 from me and hopefully it will make the top 10.', '2004-05-27 17:37:16.000000', NULL, 1),
(739653, 77436, 16004, '<td valign="top">you''ve done something to the original image, but am not sure what.  too much brightness, not enough contrast?  dunno.  do you have photoshop?  if so, try using curves - by manipulating the top and bottom ends of the curves, you can make the darker areas darker and the brighter areas brighter.  brightness is really the achilles heel here...</td>', 'you''ve done something to the original image, but am not sure what.  too much brightness, not enough contrast?  dunno.  do you have photoshop?  if so, try using curves - by manipulating the top and bottom ends of the curves, you can make the darker areas darker and the brighter areas brighter.  brightness is really the achilles heel here...', '2004-05-27 17:40:16.000000', NULL, 1),
(739661, 78025, 16004, '<td valign="top">it''s hard to find an unusual viewpoint on a spherical object - surely it looks the same no matter what angle you take the picture from...  i don''t think a golf ball is the best choice of material - although if you got in closer and cropped it so you couldn''t tell it was ball-shaped, it would be a bit more unusual.  technically, the shot has really decent focus, but methinks is a bit on the noisy side?</td>', 'it''s hard to find an unusual viewpoint on a spherical object - surely it looks the same no matter what angle you take the picture from...  i don''t think a golf ball is the best choice of material - although if you got in closer and cropped it so you couldn''t tell it was ball-shaped, it would be a bit more unusual.  technically, the shot has really decent focus, but methinks is a bit on the noisy side?', '2004-05-27 17:43:56.000000', NULL, 1),
(739674, 78037, 16004, '<td valign="top">I''m not how "unusual" a viewpoint this is, but whoo! what a great picture.  and it''s different, i guess - how yu''ve focused on the eyes is a triumph!  the detail is fantastic - it''s a remarkable picture, beautiful and unimprovable.  i like the off-centre setting, the green contrasting background, and mr peacock himself.  i am having does not meet the challenge issues, and if i didn''t, it would be a 10.  as it is, because of my indecisiveness, i''ll plump for a 9.  well done though - truly an inspiring and encouraging picture.</td>', 'I''m not how "unusual" a viewpoint this is, but whoo! what a great picture.  and it''s different, i guess - how yu''ve focused on the eyes is a triumph!  the detail is fantastic - it''s a remarkable picture, beautiful and unimprovable.  i like the off-centre setting, the green contrasting background, and mr peacock himself.  i am having does not meet the challenge issues, and if i didn''t, it would be a 10.  as it is, because of my indecisiveness, i''ll plump for a 9.  well done though - truly an inspiring and encouraging picture.', '2004-05-27 17:48:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(739675, 78357, 16004, '<td valign="top">This is great - i love the shiny blue, the sky is bright and interesting...   it certainly meets the challenge, so no problems there.  i do think the green plastic stuff does detract a wee bit...  did you consider rotating yourself round a bit to avoid it? still, it''s a well crafted image - 8.</td>', 'This is great - i love the shiny blue, the sky is bright and interesting...   it certainly meets the challenge, so no problems there.  i do think the green plastic stuff does detract a wee bit...  did you consider rotating yourself round a bit to avoid it? still, it''s a well crafted image - 8.', '2004-05-27 17:50:17.000000', NULL, 1),
(739686, 78263, 16004, '<td valign="top">I like this muchly. not entriely sure re: the unusual viewpoint factor - but everything else is lovely...  i like the way you''ve captured your models face, her being somehow interestingly thoughtful and seemingly nice...  the background, including the light through the blurry trees, is really cool.  tones are amongst the best on a monochrome image i''ve seen for quite a while...  and the graininess (intentional or not) works REALLY well.  defintely record sleeve quality.  but is it unusual enough.  dunno.  i was going to go for a 7, but the more i get drawn to it... 8.</td>', 'I like this muchly. not entriely sure re: the unusual viewpoint factor - but everything else is lovely...  i like the way you''ve captured your models face, her being somehow interestingly thoughtful and seemingly nice...  the background, including the light through the blurry trees, is really cool.  tones are amongst the best on a monochrome image i''ve seen for quite a while...  and the graininess (intentional or not) works REALLY well.  defintely record sleeve quality.  but is it unusual enough.  dunno.  i was going to go for a 7, but the more i get drawn to it... 8.', '2004-05-27 17:56:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(739688, 78363, 22046, '<td valign="top">I love the lines and colors. The tack sharp focus adds so much to this. Beautiful!</td>', 'I love the lines and colors. The tack sharp focus adds so much to this. Beautiful!', '2004-05-27 17:58:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(739690, 77494, 22046, '<td valign="top">Made me laugh. Perfect for the theme as it is rare to be looking at cows from this angle. One of my top rated images in this challenge.</td>', 'Made me laugh. Perfect for the theme as it is rare to be looking at cows from this angle. One of my top rated images in this challenge.', '2004-05-27 17:59:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(739692, 78785, 22046, '<td valign="top">How perfect for the theme. I''d be scared if I were a mouse for sure. One of my top rated photos.</td>', 'How perfect for the theme. I''d be scared if I were a mouse for sure. One of my top rated photos.', '2004-05-27 17:59:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(739699, 77494, 16004, '<td valign="top">the angle / position of the shot does seem a bit of a standard in terms of cow photography (if ever there was a specialist field)...   however, it is decidedly appealing.  i like the brightness of the colours (the biege cow, grass and sky, particularly), the lack of clutter away from the cows.  and cow noses always get the thumbs up from me.  i''m not quite as keen on the position of the sun - the shadow of the cows left ear makes it look a smidgeon unbalanced to me.  also, the cow on the right is a bit too silhouettey - can''t see the buggers eyes.  in all though - it''s great!  8.</td>', 'the angle / position of the shot does seem a bit of a standard in terms of cow photography (if ever there was a specialist field)...   however, it is decidedly appealing.  i like the brightness of the colours (the biege cow, grass and sky, particularly), the lack of clutter away from the cows.  and cow noses always get the thumbs up from me.  i''m not quite as keen on the position of the sun - the shadow of the cows left ear makes it look a smidgeon unbalanced to me.  also, the cow on the right is a bit too silhouettey - can''t see the buggers eyes.  in all though - it''s great!  8.', '2004-05-27 18:01:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(739706, 78653, 16004, '<td valign="top">i''d be interested in how you did this!  although, i must say it''s a little less unusual viewpoint, and more original presentation.  i like the image - the (i would hazard) intentionally blurry effect is really nice - and gives it a distinctive appearance compared to the other flower shots.  i''m not mad on the split screen effect though.  5.</td>', 'i''d be interested in how you did this!  although, i must say it''s a little less unusual viewpoint, and more original presentation.  i like the image - the (i would hazard) intentionally blurry effect is really nice - and gives it a distinctive appearance compared to the other flower shots.  i''m not mad on the split screen effect though.  5.', '2004-05-27 18:04:43.000000', NULL, 1),
(739717, 78355, 16004, '<td valign="top">How on gods earth did you get this wonderful shot?  i can''t begin to imagine a) where you got all those bottles and b) how you lit them so brilliantly.  this is brilliant - it''s, erm, chi is disrupted a little bit by the black disc in the centre (you could have tired cloning that out - i think it wouldn''t be a breaking of the rules) but that aside, sheer brilliance.  and it''s damned unusual in my book.  well done - 10</td>', 'How on gods earth did you get this wonderful shot?  i can''t begin to imagine a) where you got all those bottles and b) how you lit them so brilliantly.  this is brilliant - it''s, erm, chi is disrupted a little bit by the black disc in the centre (you could have tired cloning that out - i think it wouldn''t be a breaking of the rules) but that aside, sheer brilliance.  and it''s damned unusual in my book.  well done - 10', '2004-05-27 18:10:43.000000', NULL, 1),
(739721, 78597, 16004, '<td valign="top">The faded white border works superbly well against the silhouettes here - such a grand idea...  the shot is a bit too grainy i think to work effectively overall, and the bottle of water is kind of distracting.  but it''s an interesting and original shot, which is rather stylish.  i gave it a 7</td>', 'The faded white border works superbly well against the silhouettes here - such a grand idea...  the shot is a bit too grainy i think to work effectively overall, and the bottle of water is kind of distracting.  but it''s an interesting and original shot, which is rather stylish.  i gave it a 7', '2004-05-27 18:13:38.000000', NULL, 1),
(739732, 77923, 16004, '<td valign="top">i am afraid that this sort of thing has been done a bit too often to have much imapct anymore...  i guess it''s a relevant choice of word, but the capture of the subject (i.e. a sheet of paper) hasn''t been taken from a viewpoint i would consider unusual.  the quality of the print is a bit distracting too.  it''s well lit and the depth of field is good, but you could of at least rotated it 180 degrees...  3.</td>', 'i am afraid that this sort of thing has been done a bit too often to have much imapct anymore...  i guess it''s a relevant choice of word, but the capture of the subject (i.e. a sheet of paper) hasn''t been taken from a viewpoint i would consider unusual.  the quality of the print is a bit distracting too.  it''s well lit and the depth of field is good, but you could of at least rotated it 180 degrees...  3.', '2004-05-27 18:19:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(739766, 78677, 11518, '<td valign="top">LOL Yer a perv. ;-)<br/></td>', 'LOL Yer a perv. ;-)', '2004-05-27 18:48:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(739768, 78581, 9668, '<td valign="top">But you can''t see through it!</td>', 'But you can''t see through it!', '2004-05-27 18:51:14.000000', NULL, 1),
(739770, 78335, 16982, '<td valign="top">Nice idea; good angle.  More colours and more contrast would have been preferable, as well as a more interesting reflection if one was available.</td>', 'Nice idea; good angle.  More colours and more contrast would have been preferable, as well as a more interesting reflection if one was available.', '2004-05-27 18:53:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(739772, 78816, 16982, '<td valign="top">Nice photo, even if the focus is a bit soft.  You lose points because the viewpoint is not unusual enough!</td>', 'Nice photo, even if the focus is a bit soft.  You lose points because the viewpoint is not unusual enough!', '2004-05-27 18:55:10.000000', NULL, 1),
(739773, 78485, 16982, '<td valign="top">Another lovely photograph that suffers from not meeting the challenge very well.</td>', 'Another lovely photograph that suffers from not meeting the challenge very well.', '2004-05-27 18:56:08.000000', NULL, 1),
(739779, 78905, 16982, '<td valign="top">Great photo - fits the challenge well - but a bit lacking in colour.</td>', 'Great photo - fits the challenge well - but a bit lacking in colour.', '2004-05-27 19:02:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(739783, 78667, 11518, '<td valign="top">The reflection on the oven door is very distracting.</td>', 'The reflection on the oven door is very distracting.', '2004-05-27 19:04:00.000000', NULL, 1),
