(740477, 78451, 16004, '<td valign="top">of all the camera looking out of a ? in this challenge, this is a definite favourite.  you''ve been it an interesting image to look at, primarily by enhancing the shiny metallicness of the inside of the bag.  and isolating the interest (i.e. the focus) to the hand and the bit of popcorn in the immediate vicinity of the hand is also very clever.  in all, brilliant and absorbing.  10.</td>', 'of all the camera looking out of a ? in this challenge, this is a definite favourite.  you''ve been it an interesting image to look at, primarily by enhancing the shiny metallicness of the inside of the bag.  and isolating the interest (i.e. the focus) to the hand and the bit of popcorn in the immediate vicinity of the hand is also very clever.  in all, brilliant and absorbing.  10.', '2004-05-28 08:43:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(740479, 77884, 16004, '<td valign="top">i do like it; i gave it a 6.  i think i might have given a higher score, but i''m having uncomfortable issues with the sky.  it''s just too much of an unpleasant grey, and features no change in shade.  it is taken from an unusual viewpoint (i especially like how the top step appears to be without any railings).  i don''t know - i think colour would have been the preferred option (always think it''s sad to see brickwork in B&amp;W).</td>', 'i do like it; i gave it a 6.  i think i might have given a higher score, but i''m having uncomfortable issues with the sky.  it''s just too much of an unpleasant grey, and features no change in shade.  it is taken from an unusual viewpoint (i especially like how the top step appears to be without any railings).  i don''t know - i think colour would have been the preferred option (always think it''s sad to see brickwork in B&W).', '2004-05-28 08:47:26.000000', NULL, 1),
